 "_dropped_regions": "A 'neck, above the collar' region (N6) was attempted and DROPPED after visual verification: the shirt's mandarin collar rises to the jawline in this reference and no reliably separable bare-neck-skin patch exists (a first-pass box at y=0.215-0.235 measured hue 77.3, near-identical to the shirt's own pooled hue 77.5, confirming it was sampling collar fabric, not skin). A second, brighter face-skin sample was also attempted (searching the character's-left temple/upper-cheek for a flatter, more lit patch) and DROPPED: the lowest-contamination candidates found there all read median luminance ~149, matching this image's own backdrop corner samples almost exactly, and are backdrop beyond the hair silhouette, not skin - confirmed by comparing against the recorded corner_lab_medians. This repo's backdrop hue (75-85 deg) and chroma sit close enough to plausible skin/shirt values on THIS image that hue/chroma alone cannot discriminate them; only verified spatial containment inside the figure silhouette can, and no automated low-variance or brightness-biased search substitutes for that here. N6 (olive skin) is measured via the single verified face_skin region alone. Reported as a measurement, not an omission - same class as the beast palette's 'D3 has no hue band' finding.",
